                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "- You cannot rebind any keys and you have to hold to sprint.\n- You can sprint backwards. This *should* be a good thing, but I didn't discover it until level 17, namely because of the forced \"hold to sprint\", and it seems as though most of the melee enemies are balanced around the expectation that you are sprinting backwards while shooting at them in order to avoid taking chunks of damage.\n- I encountered a softlock at the start of level 7 where the door in the first room wouldn't open that, after several minutes of exploring the room, I decided to try reloading the save in case my supposed inability to leave the room was entirely not my doing (it was not, the door opened after doing this)\n- I encountered a \"corrupted save file\" issue where a save I made at the start of level 8 would immediately crash the game due to \"a missing file\", and after several unsuccessful attempts, I decided I was better off starting again at the beginning of the previous level\n- I encountered another softlock when I saved on an elevator in the same level, resulting in my \"save state\" being through the floor and falling into the void to my death which, again, resulted in needing to go back to a previous save\n- At level 10, I encountered an issue where my entire HUD disappeared including my weapon, and I was unable to fire or change weapons right at the final enemy in the exit hall. I tried reverting to my most recent save and it crashed my game, forcing me to go another save back.\n- Both of the \"rifle\" weapons play the \"shot fired\" sound effect much more rapidly than the guns will actually fire; at first I thought this was a glitch where some shots weren't counting, but after checking the ammo counter while firing, I noticed that it was only depleting on the shots that were actually firing. While this probably isn't that big a deal, it seems like something worth addressing. \n- I had yet another crash when trying to load a save on level 14; while it worked when I tried it again, with the amount of crashes I've had at this point I feel obliged to note all of them now.\n- Another crash on level 16 right before what is possibly the worst section in the game.\n\nBetween all of the above and just a general dissatisfaction with the pacing of the game, it's a no from me. If it was just the latter, I could let it go on account of that being subjective, but with the above list, it's very hard to appreciate it just because it's a niche indie game.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1790623882,
